Source: sg-shell
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), gcc-mingw-w64-x86-64, gcc-mingw-w64-i686, python3, python3-numpy, python3-pil
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/Stained-Glass-OS/sg-shell
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: sg-shell
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, wine-sg | wine, fonts-inter, fonts-liberation,
         fonts-crosextra-carlito, fonts-crosextra-caladea, fonts-cascadia-code,
         python3, sg-session
Description: Stained Glass OS shell panels (Start menu, Control Panel, Task Manager)
 Windows 10-style panels for the surfaces Wine's explorer does not provide:
 the Start menu (sg-start), the Control Panel (sg-control), Remote Desktop
 Connection (sg-mstsc) and gpresult. The taskbar's appearance is handled in
 wine-sg, not here. Panels install as PE programs under
 /usr/libexec/stained-glass/shell.
 .
 The Control Panel's administrative changes (computer name, domain, local
 accounts, time zone, update checks) are made by sg-admind, a root service
 that acts only on requests from the elevated SYSTEM account.
